re are 60 minutes in an hour.\n   - Therefore, the number of tours per hour is:\n     \\[\n     \\frac{60 \\text{ minutes}}{20 \\text{ minutes per tour}} = 3 \\text{ tours per hour}\n     \\]\n\n3. **Calculate the total number of tours per day:**\n   - The total operating time is 9 hours.\n   - Each hour, 3 tours are conducted.\n   - Therefore, the total number of tours per day is:\n     \\[\n     9 \\text{ hours} \\times 3 \\text{ tours per hour} = 27 \\text{ tours per day}\n     \\]\n\n4. **Final answer:**\n   \\[\n   \\boxed{27}\n   \\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{27}","correct":false,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:932"}
